==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
*{{l|en|her's}} {{i|now nonstandard}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hires}}, {{m|enm|heres}}, {{m|enm|hers}}, attested since the 1300s. Equivalent to {{suffix|en|her|s}} (compare {{m|en|-'s}}).<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhɜːz/|a=UK}}, unstressed {{IPA|en|/əz/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhɝz/|a=US}}, unstressed {{IPA|en|/ɚz/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-hers.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)z|s=1}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|en|pronoun|cat2=possessive pronouns|cat3=third person pronouns}}

# That which belongs to [[her]]; {{n-g|the possessive case of [[she]], used without a following noun}}. {{defdate|from 12th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|That handbag is '''hers'''. These gloves are also '''hers'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Mine is the blue one, and '''hers''' is the red one.}}
#: {{ux|en|This is a favourite song of '''hers'''.|q=''[[double possessive]]''}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1791|author=w:Ann Radcliffe|title=The Romance of the Forest|page=335|publisher=Penguin|year_published=1999
|passage=The life of La Motte, who had more than saved '''her's''' […], depended on the testimony she should give.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=31 August 2019|author=Gaby Hinsliff|journal=The Guardian
|passage=The rest of us, meanwhile, would do well to accept that one woman’s choice is just that; '''hers''' and '''hers''' alone, not the standard by which all must be judged.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} Her house or home.
#: {{ux|en|Let's go over to '''hers'''.}}

